    "['unit [unit] family [family] vlan members [vlan_id]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'switchport mode access', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\nswitchport mode access\\nswitchport access vlan 10\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Juniper command configures interface ge-1/0/0.0 as an access port in VLAN 10\\n- In Cisco, this is done with two commands:\\n  1. `switchport mode access` sets the interface as an access port\\n  2. `switchport access vlan 10` assigns the interface to VLAN 10\\n- These would be entered in interface configuration mode (e.g., `interface GigabitEthernet1/0/0`)\", 'trans_template': 'switchport mode access'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'switchport access vlan 10', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\nswitchport mode access\\nswitchport access vlan 10\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Juniper command configures interface ge-1/0/0.0 as an access port in VLAN 10\\n- In Cisco, this is done with two commands:\\n  1. `switchport mode access` sets the interface as an access port\\n  2. `switchport access vlan 10` assigns the interface to VLAN 10\\n- These would be entered in interface configuration mode (e.g., `interface GigabitEthernet1/0/0`)\", 'trans_template': 'switchport access vlan 10'}]]": 1,
