n. The equivalent of Juniper\\'s \"unit 1\" is Cisco\\'s subinterface notation (GigabitEthernet1/0/0.1). The \"vlan-id 10\" translates to \"encapsulation dot1Q 10\" in Cisco.', 'trans_template': 'ip address 10.1.1.2 255.255.255.0'}]]": 1,
    "['unit [unit_number] family [family_type] address [ip_address]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'interface GigabitEthernet1/0/0.1', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco IOS command for the Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet1/0/0.1\\n encapsulation dot1Q 10\\n ip address 10.1.1.2 255.255.255.0\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. The Cisco equivalent creates a subinterface (GigabitEthernet1/0/0.1) to handle the VLAN tagging\\n2. \"encapsulation dot1Q 10\" sets the VLAN ID to 10, matching Juniper\\'s \"vlan-id 10\"\\n3. \"ip address\" command assigns the same IP address and equivalent subnet mask (/24 becomes 255.255.255.0)', 'trans_template': 'interface GigabitEthernet1/0/0.1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'encapsulation dot1Q 10', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco IOS command for the Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet1/0/0.1\\n encapsulation dot1Q 10\\n ip address 10.1.1.2 255.255.255.0\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. The Cisco equivalent creates a subinterface (GigabitEthernet1/0/0.1) to handle the VLAN tagging\\n2. \"encapsulation dot1Q 10\" sets the VLAN ID to 10, matching Juniper\\'s \"vlan-id 10\"\\n3. \"ip address\" command assigns the same IP address and equivalent subnet mask (/24 becomes 255.255.255.0)', 'trans_template': 'encapsulation dot1Q 10'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ip address 10.1.1.2 255.255.255.0', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco IOS command for the Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet1/0/0.1\\n encapsulation dot1Q 10\\n ip address 10.1.1.2 255.255.255.0\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. The Cisco equivalent creates a subinterface (GigabitEther